
If you look ate the soruce code you will probably recognize
that its is quite staright forward "oldschool" C code. Should
compile almost everywhere.

My environment for writing code is NetBSD and compied it
also on my Raspberry running Debian and on my Notebook
in a Slackware WSL1 environment. 

It is such a simple project that i didnt do a Makefile.

ncsel requires ncurses. It might be a good idea to use 
ncursesw. Make sure you have the library and headers
installed.

Compiling.

NetBSD (and maybe other BSD ?)
gcc $(pkg-config --cflags --libs ncurses) -o ncsel ncsel.c -s -Os -Wall

Debian and Slackware
gcc -o ncsel ncsel.c -lncursesw -s -Os -Wall
or maybe without wide
gcc -o ncsel ncsel.c -lncurses -s -Os -Wall

tcc and clang should work also.

I guess thats it on most systems. 

Copy the binary somewhere in your $PATH 
Copy ncsel.1 where man can find them.
